IMPORT prelude

-- Antitrust Guidelines for the Licensing of Intellectual Property (U.S. Department of
-- Justice and Federal Trade Commission, 12 January 2017) -- THE NOUNS.
--
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW. The guidelines state when the two agencies will,
-- or will not, challenge a licensing arrangement. They "cannot remove judgment and
-- discretion in antitrust law enforcement" (1.0), and the factors they list "guide the
-- Agencies' internal analysis in exercising their prosecutorial discretion" (n.70).
-- Nothing here says what a court must hold.
--
-- Types only: no rules, no #EVAL. Every field is a fact the caller supplies. Many of
-- them are findings that the guidelines leave to the agencies (whether a restraint
-- "can be expected to contribute to an efficiency-enhancing integration", whether a
-- technology is a close substitute); those are inputs here, never computed, and each
-- says so in its comment. Market shares are NUMBERs in percent points (30 means 30
-- percent). Facts are those prevailing at the time of the conduct at issue (4.3, n.62).
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/2017-ip-licensing-guidelines.txt. Section
-- numbers are as printed; "[pdf page N]" is the page marker of that text.

§ `Antitrust Guidelines for the Licensing of Intellectual Property (2017) -- the nouns`

§§ `1.0 The property licensed`

-- 1.0 [pdf page 3]: patent, copyright, trade secret, and know-how.
-- n.8 [pdf page 3]: mask works are treated as analogous to copyright.
-- n.1 [pdf page 3]: the guidelines do not cover the antitrust treatment of trademarks.
DECLARE `Form of intellectual property` IS ONE OF
    `a patent`
    `a copyright`
    `a trade secret`
    `know-how`
    `a mask work fixed in a semiconductor chip product`
    `a trademark`

§§ `2.1 Reach of the guidelines`

-- 2.1 [pdf page 6]: two determinations the agencies make before the principles apply.
DECLARE `Determinations on the reach of the antitrust laws (2.1)` HAS
    `the agencies determine that a sufficient nexus to the United States exists to apply the antitrust laws` IS A BOOLEAN
    `considerations of international comity and foreign government involvement do not preclude investigation or enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `3.1 The concerns`

-- 3.1 [pdf pages 9-10] and Example 1 [pdf pages 8-9]: the ways a licensing arrangement
-- may harm competition among entities that would have been actual or potential
-- competitors in its absence. The caller lists those that appear in the arrangement.
DECLARE `Way a licensing arrangement may harm competition among entities in a horizontal relationship` IS ONE OF
    `facilitating market division`                                                  -- 3.1; Example 1 says "market allocation"
    `facilitating price-fixing`                                                     -- 3.1; Example 1
    `anticompetitively foreclosing access to, or significantly raising the price of, an important input` -- 3.1; n.28: an input includes outlets for distribution and sales; Example 1: "foreclose access to competing technologies"
    `facilitating coordination to increase price or reduce output`                  -- 3.1
    `preventing licensees from developing their own competing technologies`         -- Example 1

§§ `3.2 Markets`

-- 3.2 [pdf page 10]: goods (n.30: including services), technology, and research and
-- development markets.
DECLARE `Kind of relevant market` IS ONE OF
    `a goods market`
    `a technology market`
    `a research and development market`

-- 3.2.2 [pdf page 11]: technology markets, and when one is analysed.
DECLARE `Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` HAS
    `the rights to the intellectual property are marketed separately from the products in which they are used` IS A BOOLEAN  -- FALSE: n.33, licensed as an integral part of a marketed good
    `market share data or other indicia of market power are available` IS A BOOLEAN                                         -- Example 2 Discussion [pdf page 12]
    `the competing technologies appear comparably efficient` IS A BOOLEAN                                                    -- n.37: they can be used to produce close substitutes at comparable costs
    `the number of technologies in the market, the licensed technology included` IS A NUMBER

-- 3.2.3 [pdf pages 13-14]: research and development markets.
DECLARE `Research and development facts (3.2.3)` HAS
    `the arrangement may adversely affect competition to develop new or improved goods or processes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the capabilities to engage in the relevant research and development can be associated with specialized assets or characteristics of specific firms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entities have comparable capabilities and incentives to pursue research and development that is a close substitute for that of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of entities in the research and development market, the parties included` IS A NUMBER

-- 4.3 [pdf page 27] and Example 3 [pdf page 15]: an entity other than the parties that
-- may count towards "four or more independently controlled entities". Whether its
-- research and development is a close substitute is the agencies' finding (4.3 lists
-- the factors they may consider: the nature, scope and magnitude of its efforts; its
-- access to financial support, intellectual property, skilled personnel or other
-- specialized assets; its timing; its ability to commercialize innovations).
DECLARE `Other research and development entity` HAS
    `the entity` IS A STRING
    `who ultimately controls it` IS A STRING                                         -- the entity's own name if no one else controls it; two entities with one controller are not independently controlled
    `it is controlled by a party to the licensing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it possesses the required specialized assets or characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Example 3: "comparable capabilities"
    `it has the incentive to engage in research and development that is a close substitute for that of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]: a technology other than those controlled by the parties that
-- may count towards "four or more independently controlled technologies".
DECLARE `Other technology` HAS
    `the technology` IS A STRING
    `who ultimately controls it` IS A STRING                                         -- two technologies with one controller are not independently controlled
    `it is controlled by a party to the licensing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it may be substitutable for the licensed technology at a comparable cost to the user` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.3 [pdf page 26]: what "the licensor and its licensees collectively account for" is
-- summed from. Each party's own share, counted once.
DECLARE `Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` HAS
    `the licensor's share` IS A NUMBER                                               -- percent points
    `the licensees' shares` IS A LIST OF NUMBER                                      -- percent points, one per licensee

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-27]: one relevant market significantly affected by the restraint.
-- n.31 [pdf page 11]: shares in goods markets are measured as in the 2010 Horizontal
-- Merger Guidelines, sections 4 and 5.
DECLARE `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` HAS
    `the name of the market` IS A STRING
    `the kind of market` IS A `Kind of relevant market`
    `the parties' shares` IS A MAYBE `Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` -- NOTHING when market share data are unavailable or do not accurately represent competitive significance
    `the other technologies` IS A LIST OF `Other technology`                       -- read for a technology market only
    `the other entities` IS A LIST OF `Other research and development entity`      -- read for a research and development market only

§§ `3.3 Horizontal and vertical relationships`

-- 3.3 [pdf pages 16-17], n.27 [pdf page 10]: two parties to a licensing arrangement in
-- one relevant market. Each field is a finding.
DECLARE `Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` HAS
    `the market` IS A STRING
    `they would have been actual competitors in the market in the absence of the license` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is reasonably probable that one would have become a competitor of the other in the market in the absence of the licensing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN  -- n.27: a potential competitor
    `the arrangement affects activities of theirs in the market that are in a complementary relationship` IS A BOOLEAN                                      -- 3.3: a vertical component

-- 3.2.2 [pdf page 11] and 2.3 [pdf page 7]: two parties' technologies, from which
-- 3.2.2's definition of a technology market answers whether they are actual competitors
-- in it.
DECLARE `Two parties' technologies (3.2.2)` HAS
    `the other party controls a technology or good close enough a substitute to constrain significantly the exercise of market power with respect to the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 3.2.2; Example 5: "substitutable ... at comparable cost"
    `one party's technology cannot be practiced without using the other's` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                                         -- 2.3: it is "blocked"
    `either party licenses its technology to others` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                                                              -- Example 5: "not important"; read by no rule

§§ `3.4 The restraint`

-- 3.4 [pdf page 19], 5.1 [pdf page 28]: the types of restraint that have been accorded
-- per se treatment. 3.4 says "Among the restraints that have been held per se unlawful
-- are ...", and 5.1 "including ...": the list is open, so a type the text does not name
-- is the caller's to classify (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Type of restraint` IS ONE OF
    `naked price-fixing`                                                             -- 3.4; 5.1 "price-fixing"
    `an output restraint`                                                            -- 3.4; 5.1 "agreements to reduce output"
    `market division among horizontal competitors`                                   -- 3.4; 5.1 "allocation of markets or customers"
    `a group boycott of a kind accorded per se treatment`                            -- 3.4, 5.1 "certain group boycotts"
    `another type of restraint accorded per se treatment`                            -- the open end of 3.4's list
    `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment`

-- 3.4 [pdf pages 19-20], n.59 [pdf page 26].
DECLARE `Restraint in a licensing arrangement` HAS
    `the type of restraint` IS A `Type of restraint`
    `the restraint is of a kind that would always or almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.4 "facially appears"; n.59
    `the restraint can be expected to contribute to an efficiency-enhancing integration of economic activity` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3.4: the agencies' assessment
    `the restraint is reasonably related to efficiencies` IS A BOOLEAN                                                       -- 3.4 [pdf page 20]

-- 3.4 [pdf page 20], 4.2 [pdf pages 25-26]: what the agencies conclude in the rule of
-- reason. All of these are the agencies' findings.
DECLARE `Findings under the rule of reason` HAS
    `the agencies conclude that the restraint is unlikely to have an anticompetitive effect` IS A BOOLEAN                    -- 3.4 "no likely anticompetitive effects"; 4.2, on the factors of 4.1
    `it is clear that the parties could have achieved similar efficiencies by practical and significantly less restrictive means` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 4.2: not "a theoretically least restrictive alternative"
    `the restraint is reasonably necessary to achieve procompetitive efficiencies` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- 4.2
    `the duration of the restraint clearly exceeds the period needed to achieve the procompetitive efficiency` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 4.2: a factor in reasonable necessity

§§ `4.1 Market structure, coordination and foreclosure`

-- 4.1.1 [pdf pages 21-22], 5.4 [pdf page 31]: what the risk of harm is "related to".
-- The text gives no thresholds, so each is the caller's (the agencies') assessment.
DECLARE `Market characteristics (4.1.1, 5.4)` HAS
    `the relevant markets are concentrated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entry into the relevant markets is difficult` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supply and demand respond little to changes in price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restraint affects a large proportion of the relevant markets` IS A BOOLEAN       -- 4.1.1 "the proportion of the markets affected"; 5.4 "the degree of foreclosure"
    `the restraint is of long duration` IS A BOOLEAN                                      -- 4.1.1, 5.4 "the duration"
    `owners of competing technologies impose similar restraints on their licensees` IS A BOOLEAN          -- 4.1.1
    `competing licensees are subject to common restraints from a common licensor or competing licensors` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 4.1.1

§§ `4.1.2 Exclusivity`

-- 4.1.2 [pdf pages 22-24]: the terms and structure of a license. The last four fields
-- are facts that, by the text, do not by themselves make a license exclusive or
-- foreclose competition (4.1.1 [pdf page 22], 4.1.2 [pdf page 24]); no rule reads them.
DECLARE `License terms and structure (4.1.2)` HAS
    `the license by its terms is exclusive or partially exclusive, limiting the licensor's ability to license others` IS A BOOLEAN   -- e.g. a territorial or field-of-use license
    `the license is structured so that the licensor is unlikely to license others or to practice the technology itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a term of the license prevents or restrains the licensee from licensing, selling, distributing or using competing technologies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the license is structured to increase significantly the licensee's cost when it uses competing technologies` IS A BOOLEAN       -- compensation terms or other economic incentives
    `the license contains another restraint on the competitive conduct of the licensor or the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party chooses to deal with a single licensor or licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party confines its activity to a single field of use or location` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only a single licensee has chosen to take a license` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some or all of the potential licensees choose to use the licensed technology to the exclusion of other technologies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 4.1.2 [pdf page 23]: horizontal relationships, each a finding under 3.3.
DECLARE `Horizontal relationships among the parties (4.1.2)` HAS
    `there is a horizontal relationship among licensors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a horizontal relationship among licensees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a horizontal relationship between the licensor and a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `4.3 The safety zone`

-- 4.3 [pdf pages 26-28], n.58, n.62.
DECLARE `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)` HAS
    `the form of the intellectual property licensed` IS A `Form of intellectual property`
    `the restraint is in a licensing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN                                                   -- n.58
    `the restraint is related to the use of the licensed intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN                     -- n.58
    `the transfer` IS A `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)`
    `the restraint` IS A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
    `the analysis of goods markets alone would inadequately address the effects of the arrangement on competition among technologies or in research and development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant markets significantly affected by the restraint` IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`

§§ `5 Particular restraints`

-- 5.2 [pdf pages 29-30].
DECLARE `Price maintenance facts (5.2)` HAS
    `the licensor conditions the license on the resale price of the product incorporating the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement constitutes a horizontal cartel` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.3 [pdf pages 30-31]. Market power is a finding: the agencies will not presume that a
-- patent, copyright or trade secret confers it (2.2, 5.3), so the field on protection
-- is read by no rule.
DECLARE `Tying facts (5.3)` HAS
    `the license of one item is conditioned on the licensee's purchase or license of another, separate item` IS A BOOLEAN   -- another item of intellectual property, a good or a service; for a package license, another, separate intellectual property right
    `the seller has market power in the tying product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tying item is protected by a patent, copyright or trade secret` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement has an adverse effect on competition in the relevant market for the tying product or the tied product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `efficiency justifications for the arrangement outweigh its anticompetitive effects` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.4 [pdf pages 31-32].
DECLARE `Exclusive dealing facts (5.4)` HAS
    `the arrangement promotes the exploitation and development of the licensor's technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement anticompetitively forecloses the exploitation and development of, or otherwise constrains competition among, competing technologies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restraint encourages licensees to develop and market the licensed technology or specialized applications of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restraint increases licensors' incentives to develop or refine the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the restraint otherwise increases competition and enhances output in a relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.5 [pdf pages 32-33].
DECLARE `Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` HAS
    `the arrangement is among competing technologies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded firms cannot effectively compete in the relevant market for the good incorporating the licensed technologies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pool participants collectively possess market power in the relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` HAS
    `the pooling arrangement requires members to grant licenses to each other for current and future technology at minimal cost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement includes a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` HAS
    `the settlement involves the cross-licensing of intellectual property rights between horizontal competitors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the effect of the settlement is to diminish competition among entities that would have been actual or potential competitors in a relevant market in the absence of the cross-license` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are offsetting efficiencies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.6 [pdf pages 35-36].
DECLARE `Grantback facts (5.6)` HAS
    `the licensee agrees to extend to the licensor the right to use the licensee's improvements to the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grantback is exclusive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licensor has market power in a relevant technology or research and development market` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the grantback provision is likely to reduce significantly licensees' incentives to invest in improving the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it promotes dissemination of licensees' improvements to the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it increases the licensors' incentives to disseminate the licensed technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it otherwise increases competition and output in a relevant technology or research and development market` IS A BOOLEAN
    `grantback provisions in the relevant markets generally increase licensors' incentives to innovate in the first place` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 5.7 [pdf page 36], n.85 [pdf page 36]. "Exclusive" is in fact, not in form: the agencies
-- "focus on the actual practice and its effects, not on the formal terms" (4.1.2;
-- Example 10: "nominally nonexclusive ... exclusive in fact").
DECLARE `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` HAS
    `the transfer is an outright sale by the owner of all of its rights to the intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee obtains a license that in fact precludes all other persons, including the licensor, from using the licensed intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the license in substance transfers intellectual property rights, and its effect may be to substantially lessen competition in a relevant market` IS A BOOLEAN   -- n.85

§§ `6 Invalid or unenforceable rights`

-- 6 [pdf pages 37-38].
DECLARE `Enforcement of intellectual property rights (6)` HAS
    `the conduct is actual or attempted enforcement of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights enforced are invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the patent was obtained by knowing and willful fraud on the Patent and Trademark Office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the patent was obtained by inequitable conduct before the Patent and Trademark Office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all the other elements necessary to establish the charge are proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the enforcement is by sham litigation` IS A BOOLEAN
